research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md:5:The sealed nonauthor source review confirms the released output-state interface with its printed hypotheses. The author records' pending-verification statements describe the earlier release. In this separate fresh-context review, I checked reader inferences and source/evidence consistency at named locations. The source reviewer disclosed the existing checker lineage, corrected source/type/body records and post-contact supplements; neither reviewer added an independent mathematical replication. Algorithm, Correctness, Smaller-base and novelty remain OPEN.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md:7:The interface concerns proper, equal-label ordinary rooted binary trees. Restriction suppresses unary vertices, and rooted isomorphism permits sibling swaps. The result reconstructs a labelled agreement forest. The intermediate source partition Q need not itself be an agreement forest: target embeddings are checked on final F. Proper source labels and checked Q are required for the no-drop/count theorem; the executable filterMap can drop unchecked blocks.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md:9:The opposite-output reconstruction retains the actual caller guards and assumes q>0, the exact child-specific solver contract for the restricted target and whole current B source list at q−1, and a supplied positive child answer. The additional cost 1+costB counts additional components relative to the current output. Generation budget q0 is separate. The released interface includes no exact recursive solver, negative-answer scheduler, termination proof or compatible whole-original source cut union.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md:11:The conservative O(n³) materialization/selection count assumes unit-cost label equality and one evaluation of the materialized source list shared by the three owned filters. Repeated evaluations and label-bit comparisons require their own charges. The count excludes the full state checker, source generator, compiled-runtime correspondence and recursive query work.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md:13:Optional heading replacement in the sealed semantic review: replace “Independent semantic reconstruction” with “Nonauthor semantic reconstruction” when a new edition is prepared. The original heading remains part of the preserved review.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:3:The sealed documents state a conditional interface result and keep the full algorithm open. I found presentation issues in the acceptance chronology, the prominence of the positive-child-answer condition, and the ordinary-rooted conventions. These require a companion scope note before the historical author summary is reused as a current summary. I found no contradiction between the named passages and the retained types/readouts checked here; this bounded result does not repeat the earlier theorem audit.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:5:The proposed note is in PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md. All frozen documents remain unchanged. This review establishes no global algorithm, full-solver correctness, runtime, smaller-base, or novelty result. All three main milestones and novelty remain OPEN.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:9:I read TARGET-v1.md first, wrote the incremental skeleton, then read referee-sim and prose-lint completely. I also applied reading-contract, independence-bookkeeping, tool-stewardship, timing-discipline and planted-truth to the bounded evidence checks. The first batched skill display truncated; overlapping bounded reads supplied the missing text before the review proceeded. No author, other reviewer or child agent was contacted, and I inherited no author history in this review arm.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:11:This is a fresh-context assessment of reader inferences from seven specified documents. I retrieved named evidence from their exact pins. I did not rerun the 121-module kernel build, audit all originating declarations, construct a solver, or review literature. The retained compiled output is evidence retrieved from the earlier source review; reading it adds no independent mathematical replication. Background knowledge generated the objections, but no unverified external result supports a finding or novelty ruling.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:27:Line references use the unchanged files. Both manifest file hashes match TARGET-v1.md. Their lists contain 313 author entries and 338 review entries. I checked the bytes of 23 selected primary/source/receipt files against those manifests, not all entries. BOUNDED-CHECKS-v1.json retains the selected paths, hashes, exact type Expr records and named readouts; the script and log are included.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:29:Named RMAF, GroupState, GroupPriority, SelectedContinuation and FreshEveryOutputConsumerV1 sources are the sealed copies in `verification/output-state-2026-10-15/frozen-review-v1/review-v1/isolated-source-v1/`. OutputDefs, Materialize, Equivalence and ResidualConsumer are the pinned author sources in `universal233/output_state/`. The compiled type/readout record is the sealed `isolated-source-v1/FreshActualReadoutsV2.log`; BOUNDED-CHECKS-v1.json gives each full path and SHA256.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:33:The parameterized-algorithm/MAF expert represents both the borrowed algorithmic standards and the incumbent algorithm community. The phylogenetic practitioner would act on a rooted-tree agreement result. The Lean expert evaluates the borrowed formalization machinery and trust claim. The implementer would rely on the API and its work model. The beginner is the general project reader who can mistake a completed interface for completion of the overall project. These seven documents make no numerical-science or biological-data claim, so this review adds neither an experimental audience nor a new empirical acceptance test.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:35:Each objection below passes the lead and knowledge tests by naming the standard assumption the reader would check first. The sting test produced actual scope/prominence edits in the correctness rows. The novelty rows ask the incumbent question separately; their favorable rulings concern the absence and proper scoping of an innovation claim, not novelty acceptance.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:41:| Parameterized-algorithm / MAF expert | Correctness: “Your contract contains a negative-answer clause. Have you proved an exact recursive algorithm for all reached states, or only lifted a supplied positive answer? Which cuts have already been paid?” | R:3 calls the result “a conditional reconstruction from the whole current B forest”; G:5 says “The consumer assumes that exact child-specific contract.” C:16 requires “an actual positive FB answer” and says “q0 generation budget remains distinct.” | Answered in the body; positive-only scope and the two budgets are absent from the opening summary. MEDIUM, F2. Add them to the companion opening note. This is a documentation finding, not a theorem refutation. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:43:| Phylogenetic practitioner / ordinary-rooted conventions | Correctness: “Which rooted-tree convention does the theorem cover? Does your returned labelled forest also give compatible original-tree cut addresses, and is the intermediate Q itself an agreement forest?” | I:3: “The reconstructed object is a labelled agreement forest.” I:14: “Original target embeddings are checked on F inside `ForestState.agrees`”. C:18: “It is an edge in the restricted A source.” G:7 separates the “whole-original source cut set”. Ordinary restriction appears at I:5; binary shape, sibling swaps and unary suppression require the named definition spot check below. | Labelled-versus-cut distinction is prominent and correct. The rooted conventions are too implicit for an opening-only practitioner. MEDIUM, F3. State the ordinary binary model and suppression convention once; do not claim equivalence to other root conventions. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:44:| Phylogenetic practitioner / ordinary-rooted conventions | Novelty: “Is this a new phylogenetic inference method or a new guarantee for a different rooted-MAF convention?” | R:3 keeps “novelty” outside the result. G:7: “no full solver or novelty claim is made here.” | Answered for scope. No comparative or new-convention result was checked. The F3 convention sentence prevents an accidental extension to unreviewed conventions. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:45:| Lean / formalization expert | Correctness: “Are exact elaborated hypotheses, opaque/private bodies and producer identities checked, or are declaration totals being promoted to complete machine semantics? Was the claimed review pristine after source contact?” | S:3: “This review adds zero independent replications beyond the disclosed existing checker lineage.” S:11: “No other body adaptation was accepted.” P:15: “The structural body hash is a diagnostic, not a cryptographic body equivalence certificate.” P:7 calls the added fixtures “explicitly post-contact”. | The opening discloses lineage; the body preserves corrections. The S:13 heading “Independent semantic reconstruction” can still suggest a stronger independence claim. LOW, F4: propose “Nonauthor semantic reconstruction”. Full-machine/runtime acceptance is absent and remains unestablished. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:46:| Lean / formalization expert | Novelty: “Do a nonauthor replay and a larger declaration inventory establish a new algorithm or an independent formal proof lineage?” | S:3 explicitly adds “zero independent replications”; S:43 keeps “Full well-founded residual solving” and novelty open. R:7 says compact fixtures “supply no independent certification.” | Answered at the review opening and conclusion. This review adds zero independent mathematical replications. Retain the source/type adoption history; do not convert post-contact corrections into blind evidence. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:47:| Implementer relying on the API / cost model | Correctness: “Can I feed unchecked Q into filterMap, call the solver on one B piece, reuse an all-output guarantee without its caller guards, and charge O(n³) once to the entire computation?” | C:6: “Proper S and checked Q give no dropped entry”; C:16 requires the “exact child-specific whole-Bforest contract at q-1”. W:3 requires the source list “evaluated once”; W:7: “repeated invocations must each be charged.” C:18 scopes the all-output claim to “that caller's original guards.” | The API table and runtime opening answer the standard objection on their reading paths. LOW, F5: attach the once-evaluated-list qualification whenever the O(n³) summary is reused. The proposed note also promotes the positive-answer and guard requirements. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:48:| Implementer relying on the API / cost model | Novelty: “Is this an implemented faster solver or an established compiled-runtime improvement that replaces my current implementation?” | W:3: “No compiled instruction correspondence or recursive solver runtime theorem has been established.” W:11: “No whole-algorithm recurrence or base bound follows from this source-work account.” | Answered at the runtime opening and conclusion. No runtime comparison or replacement claim was checked. Preserve the explicit unknown child-query charge. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:49:| Beginner following this project | Correctness: “The author says fresh verification is pending; the review says NONAUTHOR-CONFIRMED. Which task is complete, and do these module/declaration counts mean the algorithm is proved?” | R:3: “pending fresh nonauthor verification”; G:3 still lists fresh verification and the document check as unfinished. S:3 says “NONAUTHOR-CONFIRMED for the released output-state interface, with its printed hypotheses” and keeps Algorithm, Correctness and Smaller-base open. | The chronology is recoverable only by combining historical documents. MEDIUM, F1. Add a current companion note identifying the earlier source review and this separate frame review. Inventory totals remain scoped to those records. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:59:| Source-only Q clearance versus global target-F embeddings | I:7–14 and S:17–19. The retained `agrees_iff_original` readout has checked Q and `sourceQ : pairwiseEmbeddings S Q = true`, without a target-Q guard. GroupState.lean:26–29 includes `targetEmbeddings T F`. | Answered. The global F check is retained; no target-Q premise is silently added. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:60:| False inference that Q is already an AF | S:21: “target-overlapping Q admits a suitable refining F but rejects F=Q”. The two named retained readouts have target_Q_clear=false; `target_overlap_refined` has state=true while `target_overlap_Q_invalid` has state=false. | Answered in the body. F3's companion explanation brings Q-versus-F forward. This is retrieval of compiled readouts, not a new quartet evaluation. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:61:| Checked no-drop/count versus unchecked filterMap | I:5, C:5–8, S:15/21. OutputDefs.lean:9–10 is filterMap; Materialize.lean:35–40 requires proper S and checked Q. The retained empty-block readout has Q_checked=false, additional=1 and Q_subtraction=0. | Answered. Operational acceptance of an unchecked state cannot inherit the checked length identity. Nat subtraction remains literal, including truncation. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:62:| Actual all-output OppositeSafe guards | S:31 and C:18. SelectedContinuation.lean:20–47 prints source/parent, selected-edge, good-C, cheap-acceptance and good-A-sector hypotheses and quantifies over every opposite output. FreshEveryOutputConsumerV1.lean:11–36 retains every q0/output and supplies the exact child contract separately. | Answered for this caller. Its guards do not establish rule coverage for the whole algorithm. No favorable-output filter occurs in the inspected consumer quantifier or finite list handling. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:63:| Abstract overlapping B versus actual sideOutputs evidence | S:31 and C:20. The retained group readout has B_internal_target_clear=false and actual_sideOutputs_derived=false. The actual-output receipt has output counts [0,0,0,1,1,1,1,1] for q=0…7 and internal_target_overlap_outputs=0. | Answered explicitly. The five finite returned outputs are output occurrences across five budgets; they are not five distinct partitions or evidence of an actual overlapping-B output. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:64:| Whole-B FEASIBILITY contract and positive query | I:24, G:5, S:35–37. ResidualConsumer.lean:18–21 and its retained compiled type require q>0, the whole owned B list, the exact local target, q−1 and `some FB`. GroupPriority.lean:125–129 contains both negative completeness and positive soundness; ResidualConsumer.lean:48 consumes the positive clause. | Body answer correct. F2 is a prominence correction; the definition's negative clause is not a theorem implementing recursion or scheduling negative answers. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:65:| Generation q0 versus remaining additional q / paid cuts | S:35–37 and C:16. The exact residual type keeps both q0 and q; its final additionalCost is 1+costB relative to the current source output. | Answered in the table/body. F2 promotes this distinction; generation charges are not identified with the additional query budget. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:66:| Local original edge versus whole-original cut union | C:18 and G:7. The retained actual_local_A readout gives cut=[false] on the restricted A source and local cost=1. C:18 explicitly denies the whole-source union inference. | Answered at the practitioner-facing interface opening and trace. No transport or total original cut charge was proved here. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:69:| Adoption corrections and post-contact evidence versus pristine replication | P:7,12–18,22 and S:41. The records disclose auditor/readout/parser/body-comparator/editorial failures, corrected adapters, shared earlier lineage and post-contact supplements. S:41 calls the eight false-proposition supplements “not additional blind verification credit”. | Answered and retained. This review provides no new blind-control or mathematical-replication credit. |
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:71:The machine check parsed all 72 retained readout records solely to confirm their exact agreement with the stored receipt and then asserted the named boundary cases. The receipt's 304 comparisons were retrieved and checked for count consistency; the mathematical comparisons were not rerun. The manifest lengths, selected file hashes and three retrieved exact type records were checked directly. The local controls accepted a known SHA256 clean twin, rejected an altered byte string, accepted a zero-valued readout, and rejected duplicate, malformed and empty readout banks before this script's real comparisons. They were designed after document contact and test only this comparator/parser.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:75:R:1–3 and I:1–3 distinguish an output-state/labelled-forest result from a complete algorithm. Their titles do not announce a faster algorithm. R:5–7 then puts module inventories and controls ahead of the executable guard details. A beginner can understand those inventories as trust evidence for the stated interface; no passage supports reading them as full-algorithm or compiled-runtime semantics. F1 supplies the missing historical/current status link without changing those counts.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:77:C's headline table answers the implementer's guard, whole-B, positive-answer and budget objections in the rows where those API claims appear. Its closing two lines preserve unresolved callers and all-three-OPEN status. W's first paragraph already qualifies O(n³) as once-evaluated source inspection, and its conclusion excludes the global recurrence and base. S's opening preserves assumed contracts and zero independent replications; its conclusion enumerates the remaining algorithmic obligations. P preserves the failed checks and corrections instead of presenting a pristine replay.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:79:The only potentially misleading acceptance conclusion is historical G:3 read as current prose. G:5–7 correctly states the substantive algorithm gap, but G:3 still lists source verification as pending after the sealed source review exists. The companion note should identify that language by version and identify this separate document review. No frozen conclusion should be overwritten.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:83:I performed this last, after the audience and evidence passes, treating each opening as the only text the reader sees. R:3 and I:3 successfully prevent a full-solver/global-runtime inference. They do not identify the ordinary rooted binary convention, the positive-only query reconstruction, or the historical status difference. Those omissions support F1–F3 at MEDIUM prominence severity; they do not contradict the body or the checked type.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:85:S:3 and W:3 pass the opening-only test for their own scope: source-interface confirmation with printed hypotheses, zero additional independent replications, and qualified source work. C begins with an API table and passes that reading path; G's opening needs the historical-status companion. No document supplies a conventional abstract, so the first paragraphs and headline table serve as the abstract-equivalent material for this check.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:89:PROPOSED-SCOPE-NOTE-v1.md contains the replacement opening text and one optional heading replacement. They are scope/prominence edits only. They change no theorem, guard, result, count, alpha registration or frozen record. The proposed text received a first honesty/number/parse review and a second diff-focused pass; PROSE-LINT.md records the operations and their limitations.
research/rmaf/algorithm/verification/output-state-referee-2026-10-15/referee_sim_output_state.md:91:F1–F3 remain recommendations against the historical summary's standalone reuse. F4–F5 are low-severity wording/prominence recommendations. The task authorized a new scope note and prohibited editing the frozen documents; no finding is silently marked fixed in those documents. A theorem defect, novel algorithm, kernel replay, independent proof lineage, whole-original cut reconstruction, exact recursive solver and global runtime are outside this frame review's acceptance scope.
